<Description>
<![CDATA[E300 Overload Relay Device Object]]>
<LocalizedDescription Lang="en-US">
<![CDATA[E300 Overload Relay Device Object]]>
</LocalizedDescription>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[AOI Standardization Update]]>
<LocalizedRevisionNote Lang="en-US">
<![CDATA[AOI Standardization Update]]>
</LocalizedRevisionNote>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[============================================================
Instruction Overview:
-----

This Power Device Object AOI is a tested and life-cycle managed library object for use with the E300 Electronic Overload Relay and includes the following:
- Logic to read status and diagnostic data from the device and write configuration and command data to the device.
- Provides logic interface to HMI devices so they can annunciate device status, configuration, warning, and fault data and provide control, configuration, and reset functions from the HMI.
- Standardized device state logic and a discrete device interface to provide consistent behavior from a variety of discrete devices facilitating application logic reuse.


Instruction Execution:
-----
The instruction is intended to be evaluated unconditionally in a routine that is evaluated each time the parent task is run.


Revision Notes:
-----
4.00 
- AOI Standardization Update

3.4.00 
- Anomaly fix

3.3.00 
-Added Input Parameter - 'Cfg_FailDelayTime'

3.2.00 
- Added output parameters 'Val_MotorFLA' and
'Val_PercentFLA'

3.1.00 
- Anomaly fix

3.0.00 	
- Ref_Ctrl_Inf Parameter Added
  raC_UDT_ItfAD_PwrDiscrete_Inf UDT Added
  Framework Logic Modified
1.0.00 
- Release


=============================================================== 

Disclaimer of Warranty
THE MATERIALS PROVIDED OR REFERENCED BY WAY OF THIS DOCUMENT ARE PROVIDED "AS IS" WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, EITHER EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING WITHOUT LIMITATION, ALL IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, NON-INFRINGEMENT OR OTHER VIOLATION OF RIGHTS. ROCKWELL AUTOMATION DOES NOT WARRANT OR MAKE ANY REPRESENTATIONS REGARDING THE USE, VALIDITY, ACCURACY, OR RELIABILITY OF, OR THE RESULTS OF ANY USE OF, OR OTHERWISE RESPECTING, THE MATERIALS PROVIDED OR REFERENCED BY WAY OF THIS DOCUMENT OR ANY WEB SITE LINKED TO THIS DOCUMENT 

Limitation of Liability
UNDER NO CIRCUMSTANCE (INCLUDING NEGLIGENCE AND TO THE FULLEST EXTEND PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW) WILL ROCKWELL AUTOMATION BE LIABLE FOR ANY DIRECT, INDIRECT, SPECIAL, INCIDENTAL, PUNITIVE OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES (INCLUDING WITHOUT LIMITATION, BUSINESS INTERRUPTION, DELAYS, LOSS OF DATA OR PROFIT) ARISING OUT OF THE USE OR THE INABILITY TO USE THE MATERIALS PROVIDED OR REFERENCED BY WAY OF THIS DOCUMENT EVEN IF ROCKWELL AUTOMATION HAS BEEN ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES. IF USE OF SUCH MATERIALS RESULTS IN THE NEED FOR SERVICING, REPAIR OR CORRECTION OF USER EQUIPMENT OR DATA, USER ASSUMES ANY COSTS ASSOCIATED THEREWITH.

Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved. 

===============================================================

]]>
